    {
      "id": "u_7467e7a033229c3b8325cb3e_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "To get started, the first step is to enable JSX in the list of Code languages. Go to Options → Code Notes and check the “JSX” language. Afterwards, proceed with the documentation in either __TRILIUM_PH_0__Render Note__TRILIUM_PH_1__ or __TRILIUM_PH_2__Custom Widgets__TRILIUM_PH_3__, which will both have a section on how to use the new Preact integration.",
      "sourceHash": "7467e7a033229c3b8325cb3ed8a14182a304fed3fbb15af4800cbff1162ae75d",
      "context": "Preact",
      "contextHash": "a91010572026bdddf8255cf70f8fa2ea4125bb423475c04ca7f86eee017097fe",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_8ce367ec7bc719131ed4fcd8_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "The documentation assumes prior knowledge with React or Preact. As a starting point, consider the __TRILIUM_PH_0__FreeCodeCamp course on Front End Development Libraries__TRILIUM_PH_1__ or the __TRILIUM_PH_2__Preact Tutorial__TRILIUM_PH_3__.",
      "sourceHash": "8ce367ec7bc719131ed4fcd83e24ddc325dd05e64948242136eb024867044709",
      "context": "Preact",
      "contextHash": "a91010572026bdddf8255cf70f8fa2ea4125bb423475c04ca7f86eee017097fe",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
